# Phase 1 & Phase 2 Optimization Final Report

## 1. Project Overview
This project implements a medical inference pipeline for ECG classification (MIT-BIH dataset) optimized for constrained IoT environments. The model was refactored into a modular structure:
- `models/`: Architecture definitions (`ECGNet1D`).
- `utils/`: Data loaders, evaluation metrics, and shared configuration.
- `baseline/`: Training script.
- `optimization/`: 8 distinct optimization techniques (Q1-Q5, P1-P3).

## 2. Performance Comparison Table

| ID | Technique | Accuracy | Macro F1 | Size (MB) | Inference (ms/sample) |
|:---|:---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|
| **B0** | **Baseline (FP32)** | **97.43%** | **0.8816** | **0.317** | **0.0198** |
| P1 | Unstructured Pruning (50%) | 98.01% | 0.8959 | 1.185* | 0.0191 |
| **P2** | **Structured Pruning (30%)** | **97.73%** | **0.8786** | **0.161** | **0.0161** |
| P3 | Global Magnitude Pruning (40%)| 98.21% | 0.9021 | 1.196* | 0.0189 |
| Q1 | Dynamic Quantization | 97.45% | 0.8814 | 0.293 | 0.7824** |
| Q2 | Static PTQ | 97.48% | 0.8825 | 0.295 | 0.7845** |
| Q3 | Quantization-Aware Training | 97.69% | 0.8861 | 0.295 | 0.7511** |
| **Q4** | **Weight-only (FP16)** | **97.44%** | **0.8816** | **0.168** | **0.2744** |
| Q5 | Mixed Precision (FP16+FP32) | 97.44% | 0.8817 | 0.184 | 0.3384 |

*\* Size increase in P1/P3 is due to sparse tensor storage overhead in PyTorch (requires coordinate indexing).*
*\*\* Quantization overhead (Q1/Q2/Q3) is observed on CPU/MPS; physical speedup typically requires specialized hardware kernels (INT8).*

## 3. Best Performing Models
1. **Efficiency Winner (IoT Recommend)**: **Structured Pruning (P2)**. It achieves a **49% size reduction** and **18% speedup** while slightly improving accuracy over baseline thanks to fine-tuning.
2. **Compression Winner**: **Structured Pruning (P2)** at 0.161 MB.
3. **Accuracy Winner**: **Global Magnitude Pruning (P3)** at 98.21%.

## 4. Next Steps & Recommendations
- **Phase 3 — VM Deployment**: Deploy **B0**, **P2**, and **Q4** on the three Virtual Machines (VM1: 500MB, VM2: 1GB, VM3: 2GB).
- **Phase 5 — Collective Intelligence**: Use the best models from Phase 4 across the 3 VMs to implement a multi-node voting system (Aggregator).
- **Phase 6 — Supervision**: Connect the results to ThingsBoard using the MQTT telemetry format.

